<p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500 max-w-3xl">
  The fire is banked from the shift before. Send a hand to the bellows, damper 85, stoking 60,
  feed 40, throttle shut; the bed burns through in under a minute and the drum is at working
  pressure in about three. Then take the bellows off, open the throttle — and only then put the
  load on. If the fire has gone out, the igniter at 100 lights it again.
</p>
